-       cache(1)(t"one")
+       cache(1)(t"one")

-       cache(2)(t"two")
+       cache(2)(t"two")

-       cache(3)(t"three")
+       cache(3)(t"three")

-       cache(4)(t"four")
+       cache(4)(t"four")

-       cache(1)(t"ein")    // t"one": a hit, which makes 1 the most recent
+       cache(1)(t"ein")    // t"one": a hit, which makes 1 the most recent

-       cache(5)(t"five")   // evicts 2, now the least recent
+       cache(5)(t"five")   // evicts 2, now the least recent

-       cache(2)(t"zwei")   // t"zwei": computed again
+       cache(2)(t"zwei")   // t"zwei": computed again

=       cache(2)(t"zwei")   // t"zwei": computed again
-       ```
+       ```

-       An `LruCache` holds no lock: it is for use by one thread at a time, or behind a lock of
-       the caller's.
+       Un `LruCache` no tiene ningún cerrojo: es para que lo use un hilo cada vez, o tras un
+       cerrojo de quien llama.

